# .vscodeignore — VS Code / CodeBuddy workspace filtering.
#
# Purpose (Change: fix-problems-and-smoke-deploy-docs, task 1.1):
# Keep the IDE "Problems" panel free of diagnostics that originate OUTSIDE
# this repository. When contributors open stray Go files (e.g. /tmp scratch
# files or modules from other projects), the Go language server enumerates
# them into the Problems list, producing noise unrelated to this repo.
# The globs below tell the workspace file-watcher to skip those paths so
# only files that live under this repository are analyzed.
#
# Scope: this file only affects the IDE indexing surface. It does not change
# `go build`, `go vet`, or the git working tree.

# --- outside-of-repo scratch files opened by accident -------------------------
/tmp/**
/tmp/*.go
/var/folders/**
/private/tmp/**

# --- other Go modules that share the developer's home directory --------------
# e.g. ~/cate/{cascade_test.go,model.go} — a separate module opened next to
# this workspace; not part of gb28181-simulator.
 cate/**
 cate/*.go
/cate/**
/cate/*.go

# --- build & generated artifacts (never surface diagnostics for these) ------
bin/**
build/**
web/node_modules/**
web/dist/**
docs/smoke-results.json
docs/smoke-archive/**
